# variants/base/portage/package.use/25-console — what forcing X off in the base
# costs (D24, 2026-09-26). The base sets USE="-X" so that a console image stays
# console even where an ebuild defaults X on; each line below is a REQUIRED_USE
# or dependency the resolver reported once that negative was in place, found one
# at a time (Portage reports one per run), with the reason next to it.

# imlib2 defaults `shm` on, and REQUIRED_USE is `shm? ( X )`: shared memory with
# the X server. Meaningless without one.
media-libs/imlib2 -shm

# sys-apps/bleachbit (@misc) needs gtk+:3 unconditionally, and gtk+ requires
# "|| ( X wayland )". The X backend: its Wayland one needs libepoxy[egl], which
# drags mesa and LLVM into the console image. X client libraries only, no server.
x11-libs/gtk+:3 X
# gtk+[X] requires the X side of its drawing stack.
media-libs/libepoxy X
x11-libs/cairo X
media-libs/libglvnd X
